{{!-- Everything about a carried thing that is not prose, on one ruled column — the character
      sheet's own lines: the label in the gutter, the control in the track, and a drawn rule under
      every row but the last. No rule under the foot of the list: it closes nothing, and inside a
      window that already carries a double frame it reads as a second one.

      One template for every gear, because a gear is one thing with three axes (`data/item-gear.js`)
      and the rows are those axes in order: what it does physically (the die, Blast, the armour
      value), its magical economy (what using it costs), its charges, what it holds — and then
      what it costs to carry and to buy. A Blade Called Hope shows `d6` lit and `relic` lit on the
      same sheet; a Mule shows a capacity with *petty* and *bulky* off. No axis hides behind a mode
      switch: the tag row on the ledger already says what an item is without one.

      But an axis row is drawn only when it says something. A Torch has no die, no armour, no
      magic, no charges and holds nothing, and the five rows saying so were the whole sheet; so
      `axes.*` (`item-sheet.js#_prepareContext`) is true for an axis with a VALUE, and that is the
      only test. The Add row at the foot offers the axes not on show and commits the first option
      of the one clicked (`item-sheet.js#AXES`, `open`), so a row never appears empty and the
      sheet never has to remember anything the document cannot answer; the row itself goes once
      every axis is on show. Blast and Takes Slots follow their axis as before: a rider on a die,
      a rider on a capacity.

      There is no EQUIPPED row. Equipped is not a fact about the thing — a Plate is armour 3 and
      bulky wherever it sits, but being held is true only of one character's copy at one moment — so
      it is toggled where that is true, on the carrier's own inventory line. Set Aside is the same
      kind of fact and lives on the same line. --}}
<section class="tab {{tabs.details.cssClass}}" data-group="primary" data-tab="details">
    <div class="cairn-prop-list">
        {{#if axes.damage}}
        {{!-- The die, or none. Buttons, not a dropdown: the whole range is six short words, so a
              list that has to be opened to be read hides nothing but itself — and the one in use
              is then legible from across the table. The choices come from the field's own
              `choices` with the blank LAST (`item-sheet.js#_prepareContext`): a blank die is the
              model's own "not a weapon", and since the row is only ever added with a die in it,
              that button is the one that takes the row away — so it sits at the end of the run
              with the word None on it rather than leading with an unlabelled dash. The row is its
              own, because six buttons do not fit a half-width track and a label parked out of
              the gutter breaks the column the eye runs down. The label beside a group cannot be
              a `<label for>` — a group is not one control — so the group carries its own
              `aria-label`. --}}
        <div class="cairn-field cairn-prop-row"
            data-ink="hline" data-ink-at="bottom" data-ink-w="0.9" data-ink-a="0.42" data-ink-seed="gear-damage">
            <span class="cairn-field-label">{{localize 'CAIRN.Damage'}}</span>
            <div class="cairn-choice" role="radiogroup" aria-label="{{localize 'CAIRN.Damage'}}">
                {{#each damageChoices as |die|}}
                <label class="cairn-choice-option">
                    <input type="radio" name="system.damage" value="{{die}}" {{checked (eq ../system.damage die)}} />
                    <span>{{#if die}}{{die}}{{else}}{{localize 'CAIRN.None'}}{{/if}}</span>
                </label>
                {{/each}}
            </div>
        </div>
        {{/if}}

        {{#if system.damage}}
        {{!-- Blast is a property of a weapon; without a die it means nothing, so it is drawn only
              under one. --}}
        <div class="cairn-field cairn-prop-row"
            data-ink="hline" data-ink-at="bottom" data-ink-w="0.9" data-ink-a="0.42" data-ink-seed="gear-blast">
            <label for="gear-blast-{{item.id}}">{{localize 'CAIRN.Blast'}}</label>
            {{> "systems/cairn2e/templates/parts/toggle.hbs" field="system.blast" value=system.blast
                id=(concat "gear-blast-" item.id)}}
        </div>
        {{/if}}

        {{#if axes.armor}}
        {{!-- Armour is 0-3 and nothing else, so it is four buttons instead of a number field. The
              choices come from the DataModel's own bounds, so nobody can type a 7 and be answered
              with a validation error. Zero is "not armour", and it is last in the run wearing that
              word: it is what removes the row, the same as the blank die above. --}}
        <div class="cairn-field cairn-prop-row"
            data-ink="hline" data-ink-at="bottom" data-ink-w="0.9" data-ink-a="0.42" data-ink-seed="gear-armor">
            <span class="cairn-field-label">{{localize 'CAIRN.Armor'}}</span>
            <div class="cairn-choice" role="radiogroup" aria-label="{{localize 'CAIRN.Armor'}}">
                {{#each armorChoices as |choice|}}
                <label class="cairn-choice-option">
                    <input type="radio" name="system.armor" value="{{choice.value}}" data-dtype="Number"
                        {{checked (eq ../system.armor choice.value)}} />
                    <span>{{choice.label}}</span>
                </label>
                {{/each}}
            </div>
        </div>
        {{/if}}

        {{#if axes.magic}}
        {{!-- What using it costs: nothing, a Fatigue (Spellbook), the item itself (Scroll), or a
              charge with a recharge condition (Relic) — `core-rules.md` → Magic. Three answers to
              one question, so one row, with the field's fourth choice — None — last in the run
              where the other rows keep theirs, because that is the button that takes the row away.
              The header's caption follows this row. --}}
        <div class="cairn-field cairn-prop-row"
            data-ink="hline" data-ink-at="bottom" data-ink-w="0.9" data-ink-a="0.42" data-ink-seed="gear-magic">
            <span class="cairn-field-label">{{localize 'CAIRN.Magic'}}</span>
            <div class="cairn-choice" role="radiogroup" aria-label="{{localize 'CAIRN.Magic'}}">
                {{#each magicChoices as |kind|}}
                <label class="cairn-choice-option">
                    <input type="radio" name="system.magic" value="{{kind}}" {{checked (eq ../system.magic kind)}} />
                    <span>{{localize (concat "CAIRN.MagicKind." kind)}}</span>
                </label>
                {{/each}}
            </div>
        </div>
        {{/if}}

        {{#if axes.uses}}
        {{!-- Uses is the consumable's charges — Rations 3, Bandages 3, a Torch 3, a relic's. Most
              gear is not spent by using it, so the pair is an axis like the others: it is asked
              for from the Add row, which opens it at 1 of 1, and typing a 0 into Max retires the
              row again — the number is the state, the same way a capacity of 0 retires its own.

              Text, not `type="number"`. A number input still lets a minus sign, an `e` and a
              decimal point be typed into it — `min` only refuses the SUBMIT, and being told
              "-3 is not a valid number of uses" after the fact is the wrong way to learn that a
              count has no sign. These hold digits only, enforced as they are typed and clamped
              to the field's own floor on the way out (`item-sheet.js#_attachPartListeners`); `data-dtype`
              turns the string back into a number for the update. --}}
        <div class="cairn-field cairn-prop-row cairn-prop-pair"
            data-ink="hline" data-ink-at="bottom" data-ink-w="0.9" data-ink-a="0.42" data-ink-seed="gear-uses">
            <label for="gear-uses-{{item.id}}">{{localize 'CAIRN.Uses'}}</label>
            <input id="gear-uses-{{item.id}}" class="cairn-prop-number" type="text" name="system.uses.value"
                value="{{system.uses.value}}" min="0" maxlength="4" inputmode="numeric" data-dtype="Number" />
            <label for="gear-maxuses-{{item.id}}">{{localize 'CAIRN.MaxUses'}}</label>
            <input id="gear-maxuses-{{item.id}}" class="cairn-prop-number" type="text" name="system.uses.max"
                value="{{system.uses.max}}" min="0" maxlength="4" inputmode="numeric" data-dtype="Number" />
        </div>
        {{!-- Food the wilderness procedure spends a use of at Make Camp. A mark and not a name, so
              a Warden's own hardtack counts; it rides under Uses because a Ration is eaten a use
              at a time. --}}
        <div class="cairn-field cairn-prop-row"
            data-ink="hline" data-ink-at="bottom" data-ink-w="0.9" data-ink-a="0.42" data-ink-seed="gear-ration">
            <label for="gear-ration-{{item.id}}">{{localize 'CAIRN.Ration'}}</label>
            {{> "systems/cairn2e/templates/parts/toggle.hbs" field="system.ration" value=system.ration
                id=(concat "gear-ration-" item.id)}}
        </div>
        {{/if}}

        {{#if axes.capacity}}
        {{!-- What it holds. Zero holds nothing; a Mule is 6, a bag of holding whatever the Warden
              says. A capacity makes the Contents tab appear. --}}
        <div class="cairn-field cairn-prop-row"
            data-ink="hline" data-ink-at="bottom" data-ink-w="0.9" data-ink-a="0.42" data-ink-seed="gear-capacity">
            <label for="gear-capacity-{{item.id}}">{{localize 'CAIRN.Capacity'}}</label>
            <input id="gear-capacity-{{item.id}}" class="cairn-prop-number" type="text" name="system.capacity"
                value="{{system.capacity}}" min="0" maxlength="4" inputmode="numeric" data-dtype="Number" />
        </div>
        {{/if}}

        {{#if system.isContainer}}
        {{!-- Takes Slots: the character hauls it — a bag on the back, a cart pulled with both
              hands — so it costs what any item costs, by the *petty* / *bulky* row below. Off, it
              hauls itself (a mule, a wagon), costs none, and is never under direct possession:
              such a thing is always among the character's Belongings and its Set Aside toggle is
              not offered. Drawn only for a container, as Blast only for a weapon. --}}
        <div class="cairn-field cairn-prop-row"
            data-ink="hline" data-ink-at="bottom" data-ink-w="0.9" data-ink-a="0.42" data-ink-seed="gear-takes-slots">
            <label for="gear-takes-slots-{{item.id}}" data-tooltip="{{localize 'CAIRN.TakesSlotsHint'}}">{{localize 'CAIRN.TakesSlots'}}</label>
            {{> "systems/cairn2e/templates/parts/toggle.hbs" field="system.takesSlots" value=system.takesSlots
                id=(concat "gear-takes-slots-" item.id)}}
        </div>
        {{/if}}

        {{!-- What carrying it costs of the ten, as one contiguous scale — the Armour row above is
              the same control for the same reason. Two of the buttons wear 2e's word instead of a
              digit, because *petty* IS zero and *bulky* IS two: the word teaches the rule where the
              choice is made, and the eye still reads a scale with two landmarks. Two toggles stood
              here before, which could say both at once and needed a validation clause to police
              each other; one number can say neither.

              On a container the character hauls this says what it costs on the ten (a Cart is
              bulky); on one that hauls itself it changes nothing.

              A Scroll is zero by rule — the model forces it on save — so on one the other buttons
              are drawn unavailable and the label carries the reason. They used to take the click
              and go nowhere, which reads as a broken control rather than as a rule, and the number
              they wrote sat masked in the document until the item stopped being a Scroll. The
              label beside a group cannot be a `<label for>`: a group is not one control, so the
              group carries its own `aria-label`. --}}
        <div class="cairn-field cairn-prop-row"
            data-ink="hline" data-ink-at="bottom" data-ink-w="0.9" data-ink-a="0.42" data-ink-seed="gear-slots">
            <span class="cairn-field-label"
                {{#if pettyByRule}}data-tooltip="{{localize 'CAIRN.SlotCostLocked'}}"{{/if}}>{{localize 'CAIRN.SlotCost'}}</span>
            <div class="cairn-choice" role="radiogroup" aria-label="{{localize 'CAIRN.SlotCost'}}">
                {{#each slotChoices as |choice|}}
                <label class="cairn-choice-option">
                    <input type="radio" name="system.slots" value="{{choice.value}}" data-dtype="Number"
                        {{checked (eq ../system.slots choice.value)}} {{#if choice.disabled}}disabled{{/if}} />
                    <span>{{choice.label}}</span>
                </label>
                {{/each}}
            </div>
        </div>

        {{!-- Last of the fields, and the last row only when every axis is on show: the rule under
              it is the Add row's, drawn only when there is an Add row for it to sit over. --}}
        <div class="cairn-field cairn-prop-row"
            {{#if addable.length}}data-ink="hline" data-ink-at="bottom" data-ink-w="0.9" data-ink-a="0.42" data-ink-seed="gear-trade"{{/if}}>
            <label for="gear-cost-{{item.id}}">{{localize 'CAIRN.Cost'}}</label>
            <input id="gear-cost-{{item.id}}" class="cairn-prop-number" type="text" name="system.cost"
                value="{{system.cost}}" min="0" maxlength="4" inputmode="numeric" data-dtype="Number" />
        </div>

        {{#if addable.length}}
        {{!-- The axes not on show, as the same segmented buttons the axes themselves use — one
              click draws the row, blank, and nothing is written until it is filled. Anchors,
              not radios: this is an action, not a value the form holds. --}}
        <div class="cairn-field cairn-prop-row">
            <span class="cairn-field-label">{{localize 'CAIRN.AddProperty'}}</span>
            <div class="cairn-choice" role="group" aria-label="{{localize 'CAIRN.AddProperty'}}">
                {{#each addable as |axis|}}
                <a class="cairn-choice-option" data-action="axisAdd" data-axis="{{axis.id}}">{{localize axis.label}}</a>
                {{/each}}
            </div>
        </div>
        {{/if}}
    </div>
</section>
